SN ShowLog v1.0

Response to CNet C PFile:

            $VER:  ShowLog 1.10b (07.12.94)
     (C) Copyright 1993-1994 Daniel A. Fitzgerald

     I made this out of frustration at how someone can make a utility,
install the rudest registration delay AND make the code many times larger
than need be.  Also shows the power of ARexx in certain situations...

     This ARexx script accomplishes everything the C version did, is
MUCH friendlier, is only 3.6% of the size of the C executable, took me
all of three minutes to write and, last and best of all, is FREE.

     No offense, Daniel, but if you're going to charge for a utility AND
have a registration "reminder," please make it something IMPRESSIVE and
worth the wait.

     Also, in reference to your copyright notice, I did not need to
reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble your original program.  I
wrote this from scratch out of my own noggin.  Please feel free to
utilize this code in whatever way you wish.  I impose no copyrights of
any kind on it.  Have fun, good luck and no hard feelings.

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)

 2  Add "SHOWLOG  |{#0<path>SN_ShowLog}" to your bbsmenu under either
    "2; Available everywhere" or "3; Main prompt."  Modify your online
    menu(s)) to reflect the new addition.  Note that the above { is
    actually a control-Q command.

 3  Reload your bbstext/bbsmenu via CNet's Control Panel menu (option
    #3, "Text/menu reload  RAmiga-T" and you're all set!

 4  Now everyone can see what CNet is logging about them.  Those with
    maintenance access can also view logs for users on other ports.

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

Midnight

